settings-display-help = Shown on sign-in pages and in this console; the name in URLs stays as it is.
settings-enabled-help = A disabled realm answers no logins and mints no tokens; the admin plane still works.
settings-self-registration-help = Lets anyone create an account on the sign-in page. Off, accounts come from an administrator or a federation.
settings-email-as-username-help = New accounts take the email address as their username, so people sign in with what they already know.
settings-verify-email-help = A new address must be confirmed by a mailed link before it counts as verified. Needs email to be configured.
settings-login-with-email-help = The username field on the sign-in page also accepts the account's email address.
settings-reset-password-help = Shows the forgotten-password door on the sign-in page. Needs email to be configured to actually send the link.
settings-remember-me-help = Offers a checkbox that keeps the browser session alive after the browser closes.
settings-client-registration-help = Whether applications may register themselves here, RFC 7591. Disabled hides the endpoint; open lets anyone; protected requires an initial access token.
settings-max-clients-help = How many clients self-registration may create, counted over what it created. Empty is no ceiling.
settings-requires-consent-help = A self-registered client was vetted by nobody, so each person consents before it gets anything.
settings-trusted-hosts-help = Redirect hosts a self-registered client may use. Open registration with no trusted hosts accepts any redirect target.
settings-access-lifespan-help = How long an access token stays valid, in seconds. Short is safer; clients renew with their refresh token.
settings-refresh-reuse-help = How many times one refresh token may be replayed before rotation refuses it. Zero refuses any reuse.
settings-offline-sliding-help = How long an offline grant may sleep between renewals, in seconds. Each renewal slides the window.
settings-offline-ceiling-help = The oldest an offline grant may get however often it renews, in seconds. Zero means the sliding window alone bounds it.
settings-offline-grants-help = How many live offline grants one person may hold across devices. Zero is no bound.
settings-refresh-rotation-help = Every renewal retires the refresh token it spent, so a stolen one dies at the owner's next renewal.
settings-require-par-help = Every authorization request must be pushed to the server first, RFC 9126, so the browser only ever carries a reference.
settings-ssl-help = Which requests must arrive over TLS. External spares private addresses; all refuses everything in the clear.
settings-lockout-protected-help = Repeated failed sign-ins lock the account for a while, which is what stops a guessed password.
settings-lockout-failures-help = How many failures in a row before the account locks.
settings-lockout-first-help = How long the first lockout lasts, in seconds. It grows on further failures.
settings-lockout-ceiling-help = The longest a lockout may grow to, in seconds.
settings-lockout-reset-help = A quiet spell of this long forgets the failure count, in seconds.
settings-password-policy-help = What a new password must satisfy. Editing lands in a later slice; the document is shown as held.
mail-host-help = The SMTP relay that carries this realm's mail: reset links, magic links, verification.
mail-port-help = 587 for STARTTLS, 465 for implicit TLS.
mail-from-help = The address the realm's mail claims to come from. The relay must allow it.
mail-from-name-help = The display name beside the from address.
mail-username-help = The account this server logs into the relay as. Empty sends without authentication.
mail-password-help = Stored sealed. Left blank on save, the held password is kept.
mail-implicit-tls-help = TLS from the first byte, usually port 465, instead of upgrading with STARTTLS.
realm-new-name-help = Becomes the realm's URL segment and its issuer's tail: 1 to 63 letters, digits, - or _. It cannot be renamed later.
realm-new-display-help = The human name on sign-in pages; changeable any time.
keys-reveal = Reveal
keys-hide = Hide
keys-signing-help = What this realm signs tokens with. Clients verify against the published public halves; the private halves never leave the server sealed store.
keys-encryption-help = What clients encrypt to this realm with, for request objects and encrypted tokens.
keys-rotate-help = Mints a fresh key for the chosen algorithm. The active key goes passive and keeps verifying what it signed; nothing already issued breaks.
settings-not-before-help = Tokens issued before this unix instant are refused everywhere. 0 draws no line. Raising it is the realm-wide kill switch.
settings-attributes = Attributes
settings-attributes-help = Free realm attributes, read by mappers and integrations. Values are kept as text.
settings-attr-name = name
settings-attr-value = value
settings-attr-add = Add attribute
settings-duplicated-email = Allow duplicated email
settings-duplicated-email-help = Two accounts may hold the same address. Off with login-with-email, or an address stops naming one account.
settings-edit-username = Editable username
settings-edit-username-help = People may change their own username afterwards. The identity underneath does not move.
settings-refresh-sliding = Session sliding window
settings-refresh-sliding-help = How long a signed-in session may sleep between renewals, in seconds. Empty takes the built default of 1800. Each renewal slides the window.
settings-session-ceiling = Session absolute ceiling
settings-session-ceiling-help = The oldest a signed-in session may get however often it renews, in seconds. Zero hangs no ceiling.
settings-code-lifespan = Authorization code
settings-code-lifespan-help = How long a code is redeemable, in seconds. Empty takes the built default of 60. A code is a bearer credential in a URL: keep it short.
settings-login-window = Login page window
settings-login-window-help = How long the sign-in page may sit before the attempt expires, in seconds.
settings-action-window = User action window
settings-action-window-help = How long an in-login user action, consent or an update, may sit, in seconds.
settings-action-tokens = Action tokens
settings-action-tokens-help = How long mailed action links, reset and verification, stay redeemable, in seconds.
settings-assurance = Levels of assurance
settings-assurance-help = Maps acr_values contexts to numeric levels. Empty maps none, which is an omission and not level zero.
settings-assurance-context = context
settings-assurance-level = level
settings-assurance-add = Add level
settings-registration-secret = Registration secret
settings-registration-secret-help = What protected registration is opened with. Drawing answers the secret once and keeps only the hash; forgetting closes registration until a new one is drawn.
settings-secret-draw = Draw a secret
settings-secret-forget = Forget it
settings-secret-once = Written nowhere else: copy it now or draw again.
settings-danger = Danger
settings-delete-lede = Deleting { $realm } takes its users, clients, sessions and keys with it. There is no undo.
settings-delete-own = This session's own realm cannot be deleted from here: sign into another realm first.
settings-delete-help = The schema cascades: everything keyed under the realm goes with the row. The realm your token was minted by is refused, so the plane cannot saw off its own branch.
settings-delete-realm = Delete this realm
settings-group-features = Features
features-lede = What this build carries and what is on. The gating is compile-time, so nothing here turns at runtime: rebuild or redeploy to change it.
features-on = on
features-off = compiled, off
features-not-compiled = not in this build
action-remove = Remove
action-copy = Copy
toast-refused = Refused ({ $status })
toast-hint-forbidden = The plane accepted who you are and refused what you asked: your role does not hold this capability. Re-running provision refreshes an untouched administrator role; otherwise grant the capability to a role you hold.
toast-hint-unauthorized = The session no longer stands; sign in again.
toast-realm-deleted = Realm { $realm } deleted.
toast-saved = Saved
toast-kept = Saved: { $subject }
toast-failed = Failed: { $subject } ({ $status })
